@id("close-workorder-main-with-recent-human-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Lunvick___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    output.decision: Drupe::Lunvick___get_approval_Output_decision::"GRANTED",
    output.approver_kind: Drupe::Lunvick___get_approval_Output_approver_kind::"HUMAN"
  }
};

// The approval lookup must itself be permitted, or its response is never recorded.
@id("allow-approval-lookup-lunvick")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Lunvick___get_approval", resource);

@id("allow-approval-lookup-dorvane")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Dorvane___get_approval", resource);

// Other read-only lookups.
@id("allow-read-only-lookups")
permit (principal, action in [
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_failure_codes",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_my_assigned_workorders",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_schedule_calendar",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_costs",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_kpis",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_tasks",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___list_workorders"
], resource);

// MaintData___approve_workorder (and every other mutating tool) has no permit, so it is denied by default.
```

I made three choices that affect what the policies allow.

- **Which lookup counts as proof of approval:** only `Lunvick___get_approval` does. Its `decision` and `approver_kind` are enums, so I can require `GRANTED` and `HUMAN` exactly. `Dorvane___get_approval` returns free-form strings, so I can't tell what a person-given grant looks like. The agent can still call it, but it does not unlock a close.
- **Enum literal syntax:** I wrote the enum values as entity literals (`Drupe::Lunvick___get_approval_Output_decision::"GRANTED"`), since that is how the schema types them. The reference only shows plain-string literals for output fields, so this syntax is the part most worth checking when the policies are validated.
- **Read-only tools:** I treated all the `get_*` and `list_*` tools as read-only and allowed them. `approve_workorder`, `generate_work_order`, `update_workorder`, `assign_technician` and `cancel_workorder` have no permit, so they are denied.

